      "reasoning": "Customary IHL and Additional Protocol I require that a medical unit retain its protected status only so long as it is not used to commit acts harmful to the enemy. The occupation of the top floor by an artillery observation team, the mounting of a heavy machine gun on the roof, and the storage of ammunition in the basement constitute acts harmful to the enemy, thereby removing the hospital's protection under the treaty text and the jurisprudence of the ICTY on loss of protection for medical facilities used for military purposes.",
