      "claim": "The warning issued by Calvaran forces on 9 August satisfied the requirement of an effective warning before attacking a former medical facility that had lost its protection.",
      "reasoning": "International humanitarian law obliges parties to give an effective warning to persons in the vicinity of a protected object that has lost its protection before launching an attack, unless circumstances do not permit. The radio broadcast, leaflets, and ICRC delegate notification provided clear notice and a 48‑hour period for the cessation of military use, meeting the standard set by customary IHL and the practice of the International Committee of the Red Cross.",
      "citations": []
    },
