      "claim": "The attack on 13 August was directed at a legitimate military objective because the hospital’s top floor was being used as an artillery observation post and weapons platform at the time of the strike.",
      "reasoning": "A military objective is any object which by its nature, location, purpose or use makes an effective contribution to military action and whose destruction offers a definite military advantage. The presence of an observation team directing fire and a machine gun actively engaging Calvaran troops means the top floor met both criteria, rendering it a lawful target under the principle of distinction.",
      "citations": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "The use of guided munitions aimed at the roof and top floor, avoiding the lower levels, demonstrates compliance with the principle of precaution to minimize incidental civilian harm.",
      "reasoning": "Precautionary measures require attackers to take all feasible steps to avoid or limit incidental loss of civilian life and damage to civilian objects. Selecting precision‑guided weapons and targeting only the portions of the building that housed combatants reflects adherence to this duty, as recognized in the jurisprudence of the ICC concerning proportionality and precaution.",
      "citations": []
    },
